{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories","id":1554174,"title":"Menele and Helena\u2019s Backstories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-05T15:10:48-07:00","id":1554174,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Menele and Helena\u2019s Backstories","content":"I am running a V20 game using the old 1st edition material - starting in Gary with Modius and the gang, eventually expanding out into Chicago by Night. And reading CbN, I was struck by something odd.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Menele and Helena are standins for Meneleus and Helen of Troy; what\u2019s odd is, their backstories don\u2019t line up with each other, even though each of their backstories does appear to include a version of the events of the legend. <br /> <br /> Ie, Menele was a Greek king whose wife was kidnapped by another ancient city-state and he went to war to get her back, winding up embraced as a result. And Helena runs off with Paris - er, Prias - to his far off city, sparking a similar war.<br /> <br /> But they are embraced centuries apart, and in Helena\u2019s version of the story, her husband is Minos, not Meneleus. And yet both backstories seem to strongly hint at the Trojan War resulting from each of their origin stories.<br /> <br /> These backstories are both from the same book, so I feel like these contradictions must be intentional, but I am a bit confused. I know there are some folks knowledgeable about the lore here - does anyone have any insight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T16:07:28-07:00","id":1554180,"title":"","content":"Go with the unreliable narrator troupe and things getting embellished over the long night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T16:43:37-07:00","id":1554182,"title":"","content":"Sure, that absolutely works - I guess what I am wondering is whether that is what the authors were intentionally trying to do here? Or else did they intend each backstory to actually be separate, and that over the centuries the real events were misremembered and combined into a single legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T18:32:14-07:00","id":1554185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554182#post1554182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that absolutely works - I guess what I am wondering is whether that is what the authors were intentionally trying to do here? Or else did they intend each backstory to actually be separate, and that over the centuries the real events were misremembered and combined into a single legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the latter was more the intent behind the way they handled things. But I must admit, I haven't studied the two characters especially closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T19:13:24-07:00","id":1554187,"title":"","content":"I think Mark Rein Hagen (?) was being clever here and going with the idea that they have a lot of references to the legendary characters but aren't them. They're either the inspirations for them or they are people who took their present names from the mythological characters. The latter is one I actually prefer. Neither Helena or Menele are the &quot;original&quot; but have adopted the identities due to being so old that they don't recall their original identities. <br /> <br /> Remember, the writer is aware of what he's doing because they aren't backstories that refer to Troy in the slightest. It was Carthage (which happened millennia later--Troy happened in 1148 BC and Carthage 146 BC) that was the event that destroyed Menele and Helena's relationship.<br /> <br /> If this was Requiem, it's possible both of them suffer from the fog of the ages.<br /> <br /> But it's also possible if you want to be literal that Helena and Menele did the whole Troy thing but that was a thousand years before their next breakup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2025, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T20:05:18-07:00","id":1554188,"title":"","content":"I think Menele and Helena were the inspiration for Helen of Troy and her husband Menelaus, and that Homer simply got some of the facts wrong when he told the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T21:08:28-07:00","id":1554189,"title":"","content":"I didn't know that CTPhipps, but given how deception and taking advantage of myths and legends are part of a Kindreds stock and trade. This would fit just like the Ventrue blood god Mithras taking advantage of his people's religion and taking on the identity of a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T21:15:12-07:00","id":1554191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554187#post1554187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember, the writer is aware of what he's doing because they aren't backstories that refer to Troy in the slightest. It was Carthage (which happened millennia later--Troy happened in 1148 BC and Carthage 146 BC) that was the event that destroyed Menele and Helena's relationship.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s part of what is so weird about it, actually - their backstories both do tie into the events of the Trojan War story, but in both cases, it is their origin of how they became vampires.<br /> <br /> In Menele\u2019s case, they say he was a Greek king who went to war against an unnamed city in Asia Minor after they kidnapped his wife. Due to the war, he caught the attention of a vampire patron of that unnamed city - Troile (and I feel like the name has got to be an intentional pun, right?) So the events described by Homer seem to have happened in some way - even though his wife and the other city are unnamed.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in Helena\u2019s backstory, she is said to have been forced into an arranged marriage with a king who was also a vampire named Minos. She fell in love with Prias, a prince of an unnamed city state in Asia Minor, and fled with him to his city. Minos went to war to get her back.<br /> <br /> In both cases, their mortal stories seem very directly tied to the Trojan War, and their corresponding character\u2019s place in it - but they also contradict each other. Helena is embraced centuries earlier than Menele, and in her version the king is a different guy. (Menele\u2019s wife is never named in his backstory.)<br /> <br /> Their rivalry as vampires doesn\u2019t start until Carthage - but it is very weird that they each basically have a mortal origin tied to the Trojan War, but in ways that contradict each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T00:30:53-07:00","id":1554192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories#post1554174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, Menele and Helena are standins for Meneleus and Helen of Troy; what\u2019s odd is, their backstories don\u2019t line up with each other, even though each of their backstories does appear to include a version of the events of the legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a mishmash of... things<br /> Helena was born in 1233 BCE and Embraced in 1207 BCE and she supposed to be a &quot;daugter of an Achaean king&quot;. Her beauty attracted the attention of Minos, who visited Argos and sought an audience with the king and his fabled daughter.<br /> Now in VtM Minos was a Toreador, a 4th Generation Toredor, Embraced by Arikel<br /> Helena fled when the king announced their betrothal with her handmaiden...<br /> The two women sought shelter in a sea cave and they were discovered by a prince from Asia Minor who was exploring the Aegean coast who offered them protection from Minos in his city to the east. Helena and Prias became lovers, and for the next ten years, she lived peacefully among his noble family.<br /> Minos was a vampire and not so easily deterred. He tracked the Helena into Prias' city and attacked with his soldiers, he defeated Prias and took Helena with him back to Argos where he eventually Embraced Her and fed her her own father<br /> 13 years later Prias, who survived Minos' attack raised his own army with the help of his relatives and searched for Minos and Helena, attacked them and with a sheer dumb luck Prias managed to stab Minos through the heart with a spear. Helena leapt at the opportunity to destroy her hated sire and be free from his influence. She devoured Minos's heartsblood right then and there. She offered the Embrace to Prias who turned her down but accepted to be a Ghoul.<br /> This is their story wrapped in the events of Troy<br /> <br /> Menele was Born around 1240 BCE and Embraced 1200 BCE, give or take a few years, it is a bit murky.<br /> Originally he was Meneleus of Sparta, the Grey Wolf, a scholar-king who peek the interets of Troile. For the next few centuries, Menele journeyed across Europe and Asia. In Persia, he became fascinated by the spirit plane and spent a century studying with the mystics there. He went on to India and spent another century studying with the spiritualists of that ancient land. Finally, he returned to Europe, intending to pass the rest of his immortal existence in contemplation of the astral plane.<br /> All and well, untill he met with Altamira, a barbarian philosopher of the <i>Learned Clan </i>of the 5th Generation, who was embraced the time Menele was, but we don1t really know who was her Sire<br /> She spoke of a mighty, growing city in North Africa that would put the Second City to shame and rival the First City for glory. The Cainites there would be the world's greatest, and would live in perfect harmony with the Canaille, free from the restrictions of any Prince and she was rumored to be able to cotnroll her Beast and pulled others out from their frenzy - a neat little trick if you are a Brujah<br /> Some fans thinks she was a True Brujah, but nothing really on her, but oh well, this is VtM, sometimes you have to fill the gaps<br /> Long story short, Menele was enthralled by the idea and travelled to Carthage to live there<br /> <br /> Carthage... we may never really know what <i>really </i>happened there and why, but we know a few things - Like Troile presence, the Baali infestation and other not that nice things the Brujah not really keen to talk about<br /> Many Toreador supported the Brujah's founding of Carthage, other clans were suspicious, especially the Cainites of Rome, what was controlled by an uneasy alliance of Ventrue and Malkavians<br /> Rome gathered forces and attacked, while Menele, as an experienced diplomat and a famed orator, became Carthage's envoy, trying to enlist Gangrel and Nosferato support. He also managed to draw new Toreador to the city, including...<br /> ...Helena<br /> Carthage was eventually betrayed \u2014 by a Toreador, it was said.<br /> This was actually true, Helena and Prias fought for Carthage at first, but soon Helena realized that the struggle was futile. The Romans, who were supported by Ventrue methuselahs, could not be defeated. So Helena traded her and Prias safety for important details about Carthage's defenses and the two left the city before the fatal final siege that laid waste to the city. For her help, the Ventrue rewarded Helena with the fiefdom of Pompeii.<br /> Carthage fell, Menele was away, trying to recruit help from the Gangrel of southern Africa and when he returned to his city and found only ruins.<br /> A few centuries later by sheer dumb luck - returning theme in vampire - some Gangrel\u200b gossip took him to Pompeii, the City Helena ruled that time.<br /> Menele lost it and during his frenzy he brought down a spirit of fire upon the city - quite a feat<br /> This is their story wrapped in the events of the Punic Wars and the erruption of Mount Vesuvius, the destruction of Pompeii<br /> <br /> After that, a few century of struggle Menele made a tactical retreat after Helena and Prias almost destroyed him in Spain and following Phoenician legends of a land to the west he ordered his trusted retainers to carry his body aboard a specially prepared ship and sailed westward to a new and unknown land.<br /> He began to mold the Incas into a force capable of destroying his enemy. But as time passed, he was overtaken by the feeling that the now-ancient rivalry was nothing but a useless burden upon his spirit. At last, he rejected his desire for revenge and created a civilization of great depth. In time, he began to dream of creating a new Carthage.<br /> Helena with her Aupsex managed to trace him down and to her suprsie found him on the other side of the ocean.<br /> Fascinated, she helped fund the expedition of Hern\u00e1n Cort\u00e9s and followed him over the Atlantic. Helena was accompanied by Prias and a number of her Progenies intended to provide her sustenance. Helena supported Cort\u00e9s in his conquest of the Mesoamerican cultures as her search for her nemesis continued. The Aztecs and the Spanish, like so many other cultures before them, had no idea that they were merely pawns in a gigantic game played by the methuselahs.\u200b<br /> Menele heard of newcomers ravaging the Mayan cities to the north and learned that they were Europeans, led \u2014 as he discovered to his dismay \u2014 by Helena herself. He tried to strengthen his followers, but he knew his cause was lost.<br /> \u200bHelena's conquistadores made short work of his vast empire, and Menele fled north<br /> The funny thing is, the Baali, just like in Carthage had a strong presence here too... in this case not Moloch but his broodmate, Nergal, in the guise of Huitzilopochtli - who claimed that Helena did descend into his lair beneath what would become Mexico City and she fled in terror at him in torpor, abandoning her cherished Melinda Galbraith behind<br /> Strange how the Baali are quite capable to be members of trhiving civilizations... and ancient Vampires are not that hesitant to work with them. Huitzilopochtli and his Baali worked well with Potchli's Pisanob (who may or may not a wandered away Cappadocian or member of the Drowned Legacies), the Tlacique (who are may or may not the descendants of Sutekh via Tezcatlipoca or a Drowned Legacy themselves. Tezcatlipoca for some strange reason not really displayed any Protean powers, signiture of the Tlacique, but instead had a mastery over Obtenebration or some power like that, and being able to create solid objects from darkness that withstood even sunlight. But this not really makes him a Lasombra, considering the level 9 power of Sperentis, called <b>Shadow of Apep </b>turns you into nearly indestructible giant snake of pure darkness... ) and a few Gangrel and Nosferatu, even Tzimisce wandered around there.<br /> And it.. worked.<br /> Worked enough even the local Shapeshifters, like the Balam and the Camazotz gave them a wide breath... it was a strange situation to say at least.<br /> \u200b\u200bThis is their story wrapped in the events of the rise and fall of the Maya, Inca, Olmec and Aztec Empries and the first phase of the Spanish colonization of the Americas.<br /> <br /> Menele made his way north to the shores of an immense lake. For all his preparation, the tribes there were no match for well-armed Europeans when the inevitable battle came.<br /> in 1820 the two met in a terrible showdown at Fort Dearborn. Helena was supported by Prias while Menele had found an ally in the Sauk chief Black Hawk. Eventually, they found their way in Chicago, meeting in battle on the Chicago River. The sheer violence of their thunderous blows shocked even the most seasoned warriors. Helena drove her claws deep into Menele\u2019s chest, while he crushed her skull with his own.<br /> Both were grievously wounded, and both fell into torpor, relying on their followers to protect them and prosecute their feud. Thus, it has been for the last 250 years.<br /> \u200b\u200bThis is their story wrapped in the events of the USA and Native Americans (a very briefly touched story ,but still... a story. And Mahkat\u00eawe-meshi-k\u00eahk\u00eahkwa's Black Hawk War of 1832 is something that gave the United States a run for their money)\u200b<br /> <br /> But even in torpor, the two battled on, using their incredible powers of Auspex, Dominate, and Presence to stir up people and cities against each other.<br /> After the American Civil War and the founding of Chicago, Helena focused on gaining footholds in the upper echelons of Kindred society.<br /> During the War of Chicago in 1993, which saw the city's Cainites and Garou at each other's throats, Menele remained, for the most part, as an observer. But later, he made an attempt to use the Daughters of Cacophony to manipulate Helena and to send Helena into torpor while Helena used her sway over the Malkavians to start the Great Fire, destroying many of Menele\u2019s pawns and installing Lodin as the new Prince.<br /> By the 2000s, Menele became tired of the fighting and Helena assumed the persona of &quot;Portia&quot;<br /> The ancient Brujah desired to give it all up and go back to his original pursuits of constructing an enlightened society, both of Kindred and kine. At his subtle urging, Brujah over the world have begun teaching the Path of Entelechy, an ancient Path of Enlightenment.<br /> \u200b\u200bThis is their story wrapped in the events of the next ~150 years of history<br /> <br /> <br /> In V5, Menele was drawn to the east by the Beckoning and disappeared and Critias, along with all the leaders of the Meneleans, felt their blood bond break - not a 100% proof he was destroyed, there are ways to break a Bond, especially if you are so proficient with Thaumaturgy as Menele<br /> Helena was Beconed as well, but managed to resist, still reached Tunisia<br /> The fact Menele denied her the Victory may or may not sent her in to a Frenzy, but that is certain, she massacred a score of Ashirra delegates on their way to the Vermilion Wedding and gorged herself on their vitae. The Beckoning and her battles had weakened her significantly, leaving her without access to many of her former powers. As she fought, she felt her potency withering until the call ceased entirely. This has led her to believe that diablerie will allow her to stave off the Beckoning, which she remains terrified of.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bThis is the end of their story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-06-2025, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T07:25:52-07:00","id":1554196,"title":"","content":"I guess the part that is weird to me is that both of their mortal backstories include the Trojan War stuff. According to CbN, Menele wasn\u2019t just a Spartan king, the stuff from the myth really happened while he was alive - an unnamed Asia Minor City (that is obviously meant to be Troy) took his wife, and he went to war to get her back. It was his actions during the Trojan War that led to Troile embracing him.<br /> <br /> And then meanwhile, as you note, Helena also has her version of the same myth playing out, but centuries earlier and in a way that can\u2019t match with Menele\u2019s.<br /> <br /> I suppose the easiest explanation is that both happened, and it was just 2 entirely unrelated wars between Greek City states caused by a wife being kidnapped/fleeing with her lover, but it\u2019s certainly odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T10:04:56-07:00","id":1554197,"title":"","content":"For those who actually care about the story progression of Chicago by Night's NPCs, it's interesting to note that Helena is probably doomed and we're about to see the slow degeneration of a Methuselah to wightdom. Helena was already suffering the Methuselah's Thirst in Chicago by Night 2nd Edition but that would now be implied to have coincided (coincidently?) with the death of her Touchstone, Priam.<br /> <br /> Now she's addicted to dialberie.<br /> <br /> Without even Menele's influence to keep her grounded, she's slowly losing her mind and is down to a 3 Humanity.<br /> <br /> There's no Paths to follow either (and those were recanonized) so it's very likely Chicago will be dealing with a horrific situation unless someone can get her brain straight and that is highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554196#post1554196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the part that is weird to me is that both of their mortal backstories include the Trojan War stuff. According to CbN, Menele wasn\u2019t just a Spartan king, the stuff from the myth really happened while he was alive - an unnamed Asia Minor City (that is obviously meant to be Troy) took his wife, and he went to war to get her back. It was his actions during the Trojan War that led to Troile embracing him.<br /> <br /> And then meanwhile, as you note, Helena also has her version of the same myth playing out, but centuries earlier and in a way that can\u2019t match with Menele\u2019s.<br /> <br /> I suppose the easiest explanation is that both happened, and it was just 2 entirely unrelated wars between Greek City states caused by a wife being kidnapped/fleeing with her lover, but it\u2019s certainly odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the incongruities are to help sell the idea that the Mythology of our world is incorrect and the &quot;secret history&quot; is something related but not necessarily 100%. Mark loved doing that stuff and it's better than trying to be faithful to the myths because he's establishing Unreliable Narrators and giving the STs more freedom.<br /> <br /> You could literally have Homer tying together a bunch of vampire myths into a single epic that flatters both ot them. Was he a Toreador, a ghoul, or perhaps simply vaguely in the presence of some powerful vampires?<br /> <br /> I like this but it's also something that is needlessly complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-06-2025, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T11:57:00-07:00","id":1554202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554197#post1554197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the incongruities are to help sell the idea that the Mythology of our world is incorrect and the &quot;secret history&quot; is something related but not necessarily 100%. Mark loved doing that stuff and it's better than trying to be faithful to the myths because he's establishing Unreliable Narrators and giving the STs more freedom.<br /> <br /> You could literally have Homer tying together a bunch of vampire myths into a single epic that flatters both ot them. Was he a Toreador, a ghoul, or perhaps simply vaguely in the presence of some powerful vampires?<br /> <br /> I like this but it's also something that is needlessly complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the basic idea of ancient vampires who inspired these myths, but in ways that don't necessarily make sense. I also actually rather like the 'Fog of Ages' idea from Requiem, and my players are all pretty much new to the game, so no one would be offended if that idea were brought over. So I feel like my solution to all this may be just to not go to this level of detail with it - what are the odds the players actually find any of this out anyway? <br /> <br /> Actually, to go a bit off topic, I'm half-considering really messing around with it, based on something else that just struck me. In the backstory to Chicago by Night, the event that put both Menele and Helena in torpor was a battle between the American Indians who Menele had allied with, and the American military who Helena was manipulating. I'm half-inclined to remove Menele from the mix entirely, and replace him with Nerissa Blackwater from the V5 version of Chicago by Night. Instead of two old-world methuselahs out of Greek myth, the rivalry instead becomes one between the invading Helena and the one who was already here and had the city built up around her. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T12:53:18-07:00","id":1554203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories#post1554174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am running a V20 game using the old 1st edition material - starting in Gary with Modius and the gang, eventually expanding out into Chicago by Night. And reading CbN, I was struck by something odd.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Menele and Helena are standins for Meneleus and Helen of Troy; what\u2019s odd is, their backstories don\u2019t line up with each other, even though each of their backstories does appear to include a version of the events of the legend.<br /> <br /> Ie, Menele was a Greek king whose wife was kidnapped by another ancient city-state and he went to war to get her back, winding up embraced as a result. And Helena runs off with Paris - er, Prias - to his far off city, sparking a similar war.<br /> <br /> But they are embraced centuries apart, and in Helena\u2019s version of the story, her husband is Minos, not Meneleus. And yet both backstories seem to strongly hint at the Trojan War resulting from each of their origin stories.<br /> <br /> These backstories are both from the same book, so I feel like these contradictions must be intentional, but I am a bit confused. I know there are some folks knowledgeable about the lore here - does anyone have any insight?</div> </div> </div> </div>First ed wrongfully put Menele's embrace at 900 bc IIRC, it was later corrected in Chicago 2ed more to Helena's time at 1200 bc.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T21:05:44-07:00","id":1554216,"title":"","content":"In addition with Menulas gone, his childe Critas started to realize that everything that he had done was not totally by his choice and is wondering who he is really is and if he and the Toreador elder Anabelle were to compare notes on how both of them were manipulated by the two methsaulth's over the ages.<br /> <br /> A new alliance could happen, but that is highly unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T23:23:14-07:00","id":1554219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554216#post1554216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition with Menulas gone, his childe Critas started to realize that everything that he had done was not totally by his choice and is wondering who he is really is and if he and the Toreador elder Anabelle were to compare notes on how both of them were manipulated by the two methsaulth's over the ages.<br /> <br /> A new alliance could happen, but that is highly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I liked about 5th Edition is that CBN wasn't afraid to take controversial chances with characters.<br /> <br /> The thing about 5E Critias is that without Menele's influence, he's a venal toadying politician and kiss ass to a vampire 2000 years younger than him (Jackson). Which is either a sign that Menele's brain has been driving him a LONG time or that he's a truly pathetic human being that never would have made it to Methusaleh status without his sire's influence reigning in his awful true personality.<br /> <br /> It implies that Menele used his mind control to make him a better person and the wise mentor figure that people likened to Doctor Who's protagonist was always just a reflection of Menele himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-07-2025, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T09:26:12-07:00","id":1554225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554197#post1554197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who actually care about the story progression of Chicago by Night's NPCs, it's interesting to note that Helena is probably doomed and we're about to see the slow degeneration of a Methuselah to wightdom. Helena was already suffering the Methuselah's Thirst in Chicago by Night 2nd Edition but that would now be implied to have coincided (coincidently?) with the death of her Touchstone, Priam.<br /> <br /> Now she's addicted to dialberie.<br /> <br /> Without even Menele's influence to keep her grounded, she's slowly losing her mind and is down to a 3 Humanity.<br /> <br /> There's no Paths to follow either (and those were recanonized) so it's very likely Chicago will be dealing with a horrific situation unless someone can get her brain straight and that is highly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt she will become a wight. Plenty of Methuselahs are at low Humanity and perfectly fine. In some cases even Humanity 0 doesn't do anything to them, like Baba Yaga.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T10:30:33-07:00","id":1554226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554225#post1554225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt she will become a wight. Plenty of Methuselahs are at low Humanity and perfectly fine. In some cases even Humanity 0 doesn't do anything to them, like Baba Yaga.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think that was more a mistake as Humanity 0 wasn't originally wightdom. It was just, &quot;Your PC becomes an NPC and wholly evil asshole&quot; as a game extrapolation.<br /> <br /> When did wightdom as &quot;animalistic mindless predator&quot; become a thing?<br /> <br /> We saw Ravnos go wightdom, though. Which ironically probably made him the LEAST dangerous Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> I think OPP had some speculation that Antediluvians COULD recover from wighdom unlike other people, though as part of the cyclic Gehenna thing. Seriously, I mourn so much of their stories not getting picked up on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T11:48:29-07:00","id":1554241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554226#post1554226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We saw Ravnos go wightdom, though. Which ironically probably made him the LEAST dangerous Antediluvian.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did we?<br /> I mean...<br /> A vampire who has undergone the Wassail, the Last Frenzy that koncks you down your path or humanity to 0 is known as a Wight.<br /> But...<br /> ...do you really have to udnergo the Wassail to be a Wight?<br /> A Wight for all intents and purposes is the Beast<br /> It is not unlike when a P'o take controll of a Kuei-jin or a Shadow the Wraith<br /> But for a Cainite maybe it is a bit more primal... yet, in the lore it is stated while may thinks a Wight is a ravenous monster in constant frenzy it is not always the case and the Beast is quite different<br /> In theory a Wight cannot use Disciplines that require finesse, patience, or ritual behavior... only &quot; Physical disciplines&quot;<br /> In Zapatashura's case we saw he bent reality used <i>Chimerstry </i>and those visions may or may not been high level of Auspex, Dominate and Presence (and probably Animalsim and god knows what, but many of the events are in tune with the effects of Sadhana, a form of Hindu blood sorcery which predates the prominent Hermetic Thaumaturgy of the Tremere clan by thousands of years and was basically invented by the Ravnos and Danava and maybe the Daitya) and in Time of Thin Blood he spoke Sanskrit, the ancient tongue of India<br /> You can't really survive three Bodhisattvas with sheer Fortitude and those three were not spring chicks either, Eight Thunder Sage was one of the eldest if not the eldest among the Howl of the Devil-Tiger Dharma, one of the handfull, three or four Bodhisattvas of the Dharma <i>just </i>on the verge to leave the Middle Kingdom behind reaching the Houdnred Clouds, Black Earth Boy was the Bodhisattva on the Dance of the Thrasing Dragon, master of the Jade Shintai and Yang Prana and walked with a huge two-handed jade tetsubo<br /> Rising Majestically to the Western Sun was older than Qin Shi Huang, the First Emperor of China, a Bodhisattva of the Way of the Resplendent Crane<br /> While Bodhisattvas are said to be on the level of the 4th Generation, more or less, they are way more powerfull actually<br /> Even if you put aside Kindred of the East and only work with Vampire, it simply don't adds up<br /> Zapatashura talked, used disciplines, rampaged and was angry and probably insane, but even after the wrath of three Bodhisattvas and a bath of nuclear fire (boosted up by everything and more the Technoracy had at hand) he <i>still talked ,walked, and hallucinations of pain radiated from it, like the vibrating, inner light of migraine</i><br /> This is not someone who became a Wight, not someone who lost its Humanity/Path and lost themselves to the Beast<br /> <br /> Sure inconsistentices and all, \u200bbut still... I never really belived Zapatashura lost it because of his hunger and anger and with sheer Fortitude tanked the local supernaturals, the Beast Courts, the Kuei-jin Courts, the Raktasadhu of India (the mutual alliance of the the Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, and Wu Zao against the ever-posing threat of the Kuei-jin (mostly the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India.), the Camarilla, the Ashirra, the local Sabbat and the Tzimisce Methuselah Kartarirya and her Tzimsice), Kartarirya and her brood, the local Mages, a prolonged battle with three Bodhisattvas AND to be the ground zero of when the forces of the Technocracy declared Code Ragnarok - a threat to the entire world, and authorized the use of unlimited resources to stop the disaster.<br /> I mean... do you?\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-08-2025, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T00:16:55-07:00","id":1554335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554182#post1554182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that absolutely works - I guess what I am wondering is whether that is what the authors were intentionally trying to do here? Or else did they intend each backstory to actually be separate, and that over the centuries the real events were misremembered and combined into a single legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the intent was always &quot;homonyms and some unreliable narrator at work&quot; in that while their names are clear winks to the Illiad, their pre- and early embrace years much less so, <b>specially </b>in the case of Helena (mind-boggling Appearance notwithstanding) whose backstory with Prias diverges immensely from anything like Homer's epic as we know it.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Critias - is he supposed to be the uncle of Plato that was part of the thirty tyrants of Athens, his grandfather of the same name that figures as a character in Plato's dialogues about Atlantis (Enoch?!), a pseudonym adopted by Socrates upon faking suicide after his embrace or neither of these - and pretty much anyone else in CbN, might be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2025, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T05:08:20-07:00","id":1554342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554174-menele-and-helena\u2019s-backstories?p=1554335#post1554335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the intent was always &quot;homonyms and some unreliable narrator at work&quot; in that while their names are clear winks to the Illiad, their pre- and early embrace years much less so, <b>specially </b>in the case of Helena (mind-boggling Appearance notwithstanding) whose backstory with Prias diverges immensely from anything like Homer's epic as we know it.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Critias - is he supposed to be the uncle of Plato that was part of the twelve tyrants of Athens, his grandfather of the same name that figures as a character in Plato's dialogues about Atlantis (Enoch?!), a pseudonym adopted by Socrates upon faking suicide after his embrace or neither of these - and pretty much anyone else in CbN, might be said.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on Critias is he was a Sophist rather than Socrates and just Critias.<br /> <br /> Not someone actually famous but in the general vicinity of a bunch of very famous people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T08:11:07-07:00","id":1554343,"title":"","content":"Making the kindred silent and mostly unseen witness &amp; participants of the history is quite practical and valid a take.<br /> <br /> With Critias in my current chronicle i <i>sort of</i> danced around this issue by making him the same as the character in Plato's dialogue (that may, or not, be the same as the oligarch of the thirty tyrants or his grandfather instead), because bringing the tale of Atlantis as a possible non-biblical take on kindred myths usually associated with the Book of Nod was just too juicy to ignore.<br /> <br /> That Critias is actually name-dropped in Aristotle DeLaurent's notes to the Book of Nod only made a stronger case for playing him as connected to crypto-noddism in an understated manner - in fact he takes part of the role filled by Vitel in my current chronicle's version of the events described in BJD.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, since i pretty much ignored the Revised era conceit of the Sabbat taking over the city - the sect's post-&quot;Firedance&quot; center in the US and Vykos main base actually being Detroit instead in my own crypto-continuity - Vitel is still very much around as Camarilla prince of DC, if he has been outed as Lasombra or not still unmentioned so far)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2025, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}